Two failures found and fixed while producing this log
-----------------------------------------------------
1. First concurrency attempt reported +23 (A=16, B=7). Cause was NOT lost writes:
   store() dedups at cosine >= 0.95 and the templated probe texts scored
   0.9540-0.9575 (see dedup_audit.log near_dup lines). Probe rewritten to six
   unrelated sentence frames; per-write get(name) verification added.
2. Second attempt reported +49 with
   "LockTimeoutError: store lock /tmp/r60b/shared.mpmf.lock not acquired within 10.0s":
   store() embeds INSIDE the flock, so 25 sequential writes hold the lock ~25 s and
   starve the other writer. Default wait raised to 60 s, overridable with
   $MPMF_STORE_LOCK_TIMEOUT (memory.py:_write_txn_open).
3. The live box's /root/.mpmf/health/dedup_audit.log received the scratch probes'
   near_dup lines, because DEDUP_AUDIT_LOG was a hardcoded /root path. Fixed in
   r60c: audit_log_path() resolves $MPMF_HOME/health/dedup_audit.log and creates
   the directory; regression test tests/test_dedup_audit_log.py.
